---
export const title = 'Accessibility';
export const order = 300;
---

<p>
  A screen reader reads the tile as one sentence: the label, the formatted value and the change, for
  example "Monthly revenue, $12,400, up 8% vs last month". Without a <code>comparison</code> the
  sentence ends "from last period". While <code>loading</code>, the tile is busy and reads its label
  and "Loading". The <code>help</code> button is named "About this metric" and described by the help
  text in its tooltip.
</p>
<p>
  The strings are translated with <code>setPeacockStrings()</code>: <code>statUp</code>,
  <code>statDown</code>, <code>statUnchanged</code>, <code>statComparison</code>,
  <code>statHelp</code>, <code>notSet</code> and the shared <code>loading</code>.
</p>
